<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 50 mln stg late help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 50 mln stg late help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with around 50 million stg of unspecified late assistance.  </p>
<p>			    EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    500 MLN    450 MLN    300 MLN    300 MLN</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    =	     50 MLN    250 MLN    300 MLN</p>
<p>DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS   =	     50 MLN*   200 MLN*</p>
<p> LATE ASSISTANCE						   50 MLN</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-15/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
